WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.070
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:07.750
As you will see in many a comments section,
being first is very important to some people.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:12.400
We’re a competitive race us humans and there’s
a never ending battle to be number one on

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.550
the list, whether it’s for lightning fast
speeds, vast sums of money, or eating a frankly

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.230
worrying volume of food in a short time.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.980
And once your name is in the history books,
it’s there for good.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:28.519
But that’s no guarantee that the general
population will have any idea who the hell

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:29.519
you are.

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:33.800
Sure, we know the first man on the moon, the
first people to fly.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:39.120
But other firsts become lost to the darkest
corners of Wikipedia.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.680
So today we’re looking at some little known
but astonishingly interesting firsts from

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.420
history.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:52.149
Let’s start on a nice depressing war.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:57.660
When all the dust has settled, the historians
wander in, stretching their leather elbow

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.289
patches, and try to work out what on Earth
happened.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:07.909
So, in a war involving so many millions of
deaths, does any one individual casualty have

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:10.970
more importance than the others?

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.420
Well, maybe.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:19.799
Franciszek Honiok could be described as the
first casualty of WW2 but he is much more

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:21.170
important than that.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:25.930
Germany and Poland had an ongoing dispute
over their border and the Nazis, not renowned

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:30.320
for their patience, decided to take matters
into their own hands.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.920
Honiok was an unmarried German farmer, with
Polish sympathies.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:41.080
On 30th August 1939, in the village of Polomia,
he was arrested by the SS.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:46.729
The next day, this SS squad dressed as Polish
saboteurs and stormed a radio station in the

00:01:46.729 --> 00:01:50.840
city of Gliwice and fired shots in the air.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.780
One German officer grabbed the microphone
and shouted in Polish “Attention!

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.850
This is Gliwice.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.970
The broadcasting station is in Polish hands”.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:05.570
They then left Honiok’s body, who they had
already killed by injection, and filled him

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.170
with bullet holes.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:11.250
They also added the bodies of other dead Germans,
dressed as Polish soldiers, which they had

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.250
brought from a local concentration camp.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:17.100
These bodies were then presented as evidence
that the Polish were attacking and the messaged

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.230
that was screamed into the microphone was
broadcast across the country.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:26.050
Honiok’s death was used to justify the start
of the war.

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:28.750
Nazi propaganda at its best.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:34.720
The following morning, on 1st September 1939,
Hitler declared war on Poland.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:40.680
I mean, it’s probably been said before,
but the Nazis really were a bunch of bastards.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.240
Although there are still some inequalities
in the world today, at least there has been

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.980
some improvement in the number of women in
powerful positions and we now have women leading

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.511
Britain and Germany and potentially America.

00:02:51.511 --> 00:02:57.900
But historically, we have not really let women
up at the top table, possibly because we were

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.320
embarrassed that we had got it so messy and
now we’d have to bother to put our pants

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.320
on.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:08.180
There have been famous queens such as Cleopatra,
Catherine the Great and Victoria but when

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:14.420
it came to proper non-royal leaders, it took
quite some time for one to appear.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:19.840
Khertek Anchimaa-Toka was the first female
leader of the modern world.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:25.010
In 1940, she was made Chair of the Presidium
of Little Khural, meaning she was the head

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.840
of the Tuvan People’s Republic.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.230
Tuva is now part of Russia but it was a member
of the Soviet Union.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:34.900
When Anchimaa-Toka, was born, Tuva was just
beginning to form, having previously been

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.310
part of the Chinese empire.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:43.470
The Bolsheviks helped set up the Tuvan People’s
Republic after the Russian revolution of 1917.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:48.590
The new state helped women to read and write,
since most were illiterate and Anchimaa-Toka

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:52.300
was one of the first to learn the new Tuvan
alphabet.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:58.130
She then worked to help others gain an education
and eventually won a place in a Moscow university,

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:03.210
where she adopted Stalinist ideology, which
was pretty important since if you weren’t

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:09.970
a member of the Stalin fan club, things like
your dinner, family and life often got misplaced

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:10.970
somehow.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:16.160
Of course, it’s not just politics where
women have been under-represented, it’s

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.000
in the arts too.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:24.860
In 2009, Kathryn Bigelow became the first
woman to win Best Director in 80 years of

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.520
the Oscar awards.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:32.120
Hurt Locker was the gritty story of a bomb
disposal team in Iraq but, despite its brilliance,

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.520
it only took $12 million at the box office.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:41.850
Ironically, it beat Avatar in the Oscar race,
directed by Bigelow’s ex-husband James Cameron,

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.700
which is the highest grossing film of all
time.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:49.510
Bigelow had a previous box office smash with
Point Break, where she tried numerous times

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:54.920
to kill off Keanu Reeves by throwing him out
of planes and sending him off into giant waves

00:04:54.920 --> 00:05:00.310
but unfortunately she was unsuccessful and
had to allow him continue to act.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:04.830
The film is such a cult classic that there
is now a touring stage show called Point Break

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:06.010
Live.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:10.260
Since they didn’t have a spare broomstick
to act Keanu’s part, they fill it every

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.580
night with a different member of the audience.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:17.370
Julia Phillips was actually the first woman
to win an Oscar for best film, when she was

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.650
a producer on the classic conman tale The
Sting.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:26.280
Other notable Oscar firsts are; Hattie McDaniel,
the first black Oscar winner as supporting

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:31.590
actress in Gone With The Wind and, of course,
Leonardo DiCaprio who probably deserves a

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:38.230
mention as the most historically unsuccessful
nominee to finally win an Oscar, it’s a

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:42.460
good job he did before he eventually snapped
and went all “Man-vs-Bear” on the audience.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:48.210
We can’t talk about firsts without talking
about sport, and where better to look than

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.520
the Olympics.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:55.860
The modern Olympics was first held in Athens
and American James Connolly won the very first

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.310
gold medal for the triple jump.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:04.139
The 100m has often been the headline act and
Jim Hines holds the official record as first

00:06:04.139 --> 00:06:10.320
man to run it in under ten seconds, with 9.95
in the 1968 final.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:16.020
There had been other sub ten times before,
with American Bob Hayes being the first to

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:22.110
ever make it on paper, but a rule change about
timing and wind speeds in 1977 meant that

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.620
these are no longer recognized.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:30.890
Physicists think it’s unlikely the world
record will ever go much below 9.4 seconds

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:37.310
and, surprisingly, the best hope is actually
the Paralympics, since the blades, made famous

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:43.240
by Oscar Pistorius, are lighter than a leg
and can increase the time connected with the

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:45.730
ground and so apply more force.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:49.610
And finally, let’s talk about love.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:57.120
On 1st April 2001, Helene Faasen and Anne-Marie
thus became the first gay couple to get married

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.470
in the modern era, along with three other
pairs of gay men.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:05.451
The wedding took place in Amsterdam and since
then we have seen about 20 countries follow

00:07:05.451 --> 00:07:07.450
suit by making it legal.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:11.020
The thing is, gay marriage is not a new thing
at all.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:16.180
No one batted an eyelid when Roman Emperor
Nero completed a love triangle by marrying

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:22.780
a freedman called Pythagoras and later a young
boy called Sporus, presumably chosen for his

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:28.910
small size so the sum of him and Nero squared
was equal to Pythagoras squared.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:34.282
There’s also Pedro Díaz and Muño Vandilaz,
two men married in a Galician church in 1061.

00:07:34.282 --> 00:07:41.630
And let’s not forget the Siwa Oasis in Egypt
which used to have its own form of same-sex

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:42.630
marriage.

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:47.850
So, with so many of the firsts already ticked
off the list, you’re going to have to get

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:50.920
creative if you want to join the annals of
the greats.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:54.620
Maybe try inventing your own sport or developing
your own language.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:08:00.530
Or, if you want to be a real maverick, start
preparing to be the first person to buy the

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:05.919
revolutionary iPhone 8, which will feature
no headphone jack and no screen.

00:08:05.919 --> 00:08:21.700
You’ll be paying more for less, sure people
will think you’re crazy, but at least you’ll

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:24.389
be first.

00:08:24.389 --> 00:08:31.950
Thanks for the view, subscribe for more Thoughty2.

